  "kind": "protocol_ir",
  "id": "ipsc_triculture_single_cell_capsule_rnaseq",
  "name": "iPSC tri-culture to capsule-based single-cell RNA library",
  "goal": "Grow iPSC-derived neurons, microglia and astrocytes side by side (first apart, then sharing medium), then encapsulate single cells in semi-permeable hydrogel capsules, lyse, reverse transcribe, split into four index-PCR sublibraries, release the cDNA and clean up the library with magnetic beads for sequencing.",
  "source": {
    "kind": "prompt",
    "file": null,
    "title": "Grow three iPSC-derived cell types (neurons, microglia, astrocytes) side by...",
    "citation": null
  },
  "placeholder": true,
  "assumptions": [
    "No written protocol was given; the full step list is expanded from standard published methods.",
    "Added steps: separate and shared-medium culture details, quench, centrifuge, resuspend, filter, count, post-emulsion-break oil wash, post-cure wash, post-lysis wash, post-RT wash, pooling and final QC.",
    "Culture durations, dissociation time and temperature, centrifuge speed, volumes, curing time, 405 nm curing light and wash repeat counts are typical stand-in values.",
    "Lysis, reverse transcription, index PCR and enzymatic release times, temperatures and cycle numbers are left as placeholders for the lab to set.",
    "The order break emulsion then cure follows the goal text; the capsules are taken to be collected into aqueous phase after the emulsion is broken.",
    "Magnetic bead clean-up is written out as bind, wash on magnet and elute.",
    "Reagent identities (shell polymer, oil, enzymes, buffers) are generic assumptions."
